&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;ASM is a leading global provider of products, services, and materials for semiconductor processing. Innovation has been at the heart of everything we do for over half a century. The brilliant minds at ASM are dedicated to developing groundbreaking solutions for the world&#39;s leading semiconductor manufacturers. Every day, we drive the development of next-generation computer chip technologies, staying a few steps ahead of the future. Our talented and enthusiastic employees are just like you: committed to improving people&#39;s lives and unlocking new possibilities. Through a collaborative approach to research and development, we advance key semiconductor technologies and platforms such as ALD, epitaxy, PEALD, PECVD, and vertical furnaces. We have also recently entered the promising growth market of silicon carbide epitaxy. Year after year, our innovations help make chips smaller, faster, and more powerful. In fact, you can find our technology in every aspect of modern life: in artificial intelligence, medical devices, 5G, smartphones, autonomous driving, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing installations, implementing new developments, and conducting qualification procedures, as well as carrying out preventive and corrective maintenance on complex electronic/electromechanical semiconductor equipment at ASM customer sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing repairs during equipment downtime, collaborating in diverse teams, and developing and presenting proposed solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working on-site at various customer locations within cleanroom environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to travel: Within the ASM Europe region, we have many customers spread across the entire area. Therefore, a willingness to travel for business—both within Germany and to other European countries—is a requirement. Due to ASM’s growing international presence and expanding customer base, occasional business trips to North America or Asia may also be necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Profile:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or Electronics (or equivalent knowledge); applications from certified master craftsmen and technicians are also welcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using measuring instruments and hand tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills (German and English)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in MS Office; SAP knowledge is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ideal candidate brings initial professional experience in field service or customer support and has gained experience in the assembly and commissioning of systems, preferably within the semiconductor industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We also welcome applications from suitable entry-level candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Class B driver’s license mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer at ASM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to work for a leading provider of semiconductor process equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A varied and dynamic international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An attractive salary package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company car for business and private use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At ASM, we are committed to supporting our employees and empowering them to develop their talents and perform at their best. We actively foster an inclusive and diverse culture built on trust and transparency. Our people are our strength, and we value the differences each individual brings, as they make us a better team. By embracing a wide range of perspectives, we cultivate a culture of continuous exploration and the adoption of new ideas. At every step, we recognize that it is our valued employees who enable us to deliver outstanding products and services to our customers—and to make a positive impact on society.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us on our journey. Discover how you can be part of our exciting future and apply today! To learn more about ASM, visit us at asm.com and on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;To learn more about ASM, find us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asm.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;asm.com&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/asm/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ASMOfficialCompany&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/asmofficialcompany/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ASMofficialco&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/ASM_Official&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Residency in Germany is required. This role is currently fully remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Solution Architect &lt;/strong&gt;to be on the front lines, working closely with our customers and prospects, guiding them on how to build robust DevSecOps processes. You will work with our sales, product, customer success &amp;amp; engineering teams to help customers understand the value of JFrog Solution from a technical and business perspective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love working with brilliant people, being part of an energetic team and changing the world of software, you might be the perfect Frog to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Solution Architect, New Logo in JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner and Collaborate with account executives to understand customer requirements and propose customized technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives into technical requirements and solution designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct discovery sessions, technical presentations, and product demonstrations for prospective customers in both English and German.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct compelling Proof of Values (POVs), and product demonstrations to showcase the value and impact of JFrog solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support transition from pre-sales to post-sales, ensuring continuity and alignment of expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to RFPs, RFIs, and technical questionnaires, including those in German-speaking markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent JFrog at industry events and conferences, highlighting the transformative potential of JFrog products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence JFrog’s product roadmap by communicating customer feedback and identifying trends in the DevOps and DevSecOps landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of industry trends, continuously enhancing your knowledge of emerging technologies in DevOps, cloud infrastructure, and software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Solution Architect, New Logo in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10+ years of experience in technical sales, presales, or sales engineering roles (experience with MEDDPICC is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in DevOps tools and methodologies, including Docker, Kubernetes, CI servers, Git, Artifactory, and build tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building software pipelines using diverse DevOps tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience&lt;/strong&gt; with Linux and cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP) – mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software architecture design, scalable product development, and on-premise/cloud hybrid environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering POVs and technical demonstrations to diverse stakeholders, from technical teams to business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-centric mindset with a &quot;can-do&quot; attitude and a passion for learning and solving complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and presentation skills, capable of translating technical concepts into business value for varied audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Pantheon has been at the forefront of private markets investing for more than 40 years, earning a reputation for an innovative approach to investing in secondaries, co-investments, and primary fund investments, as well as capital formation across commingled funds, evergreen vehicles and customized solutions. Our specialist investment capabilities span multiple strategies across private equity, infrastructure and real assets, and private credit. Through our collaborative and committed culture, we find new ways to solve complex problems together and deliver innovative investment opportunities across private markets. Pantheon currently manages approximately $82.3 billion in AUM across all its strategies, serving more than 750 institutional and 638 private wealth clients worldwide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For further details please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.pantheon.com&quot;&gt;www.pantheon.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Global Investor Services, the Investor Services Senior Associate is a senior operational role responsible for improving the end to-end client experience and strengthening the effectiveness of the Client Solutions function. The role combines client service delivery, process ownership, data governance, systems improvement and line management of one Analyst within the Investor Services team. Working as part of the global client solutions team, the Senior Associate will act as a key coordination point between Investor Services, Client Solutions, internal specialist functions and external service providers. The role will require close collaboration across the business and with third-party partners to support client lifecycle activity, regulatory and tax documentation, due diligence, screening and process improvement. It will also contribute to the continued development and integration of client-facing and internal systems, including the CRM and Investor Portal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Investor Services and client requirements in internal forums, working groups and cross-functional initiatives focused on improving global client processes and service delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of Global Investor Services and the Change Office to identify, plan and deliver local and global projects that simplify, improve and automate client service activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of the Investor Services Analyst by setting clear objectives, providing guidance and feedback, sharing knowledge, and helping to build capability across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Process and Service Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and execute core client lifecycle processes, including onboarding, offboarding, transfers of interest, fund extensions, fund terminations, tax repapering, KYC refreshes and World-Check activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with external fund administrators, tax consultants, and compliance service providers to coordinate client documentation, due diligence, screening and related process activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain oversight of global client service activity to ensure processes are consistent, well controlled and aligned with business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage non-standard internal client data requests and client-related projects, ensuring priorities, ownership and next steps are clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee ad-hoc client communications and administrative activity where central coordination is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Experience and Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements to global client processes, identifying opportunities to make the client experience more consistent, efficient and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce, maintain and coordinate delivery of the global client service plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Reporting to improve client support, maintain reporting standards and contribute to continued reporting development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation of Tier 3 client support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems, Data and Process Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technology teams and the Change Office to drive developments and integration of existing client facing and internal IR support systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify Investor and Client Solutions processes for systemization and integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree-level education (or equivalent experience) is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of asset management&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; the private markets industry, including investor servicing, fund operations and the client lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in client service or investor-facing support, with a strong understanding of how to deliver a high-quality client experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with client due diligence, KYC refreshes, tax documentation processes and screening tools such as World-Check would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build relationships, influence stakeholders and work effectively across functions and seniority levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering short and long-term projects, with evidence of clear outcomes, strong execution and practical process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting, coaching or managing team members, including setting objectives and providing constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High levels of professionalism, confidentiality, discretion and judgement when handling client, investor and business information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, work under pressure and deliver to deadlines with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present information clearly and adapt messaging for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems capability, including proficiency in Excel, PowerPoint and CRM platforms; experience with investor portals or data management tools would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
